   "projection_text": "NBP March projection (4 Mar; data to 19 Feb, war excluded): CPI 50% bands 1.6-2.9% (2026), 1.1-3.7% (2027).",
   "fiscal_text": "2025 general-government deficit ~7.0% of GDP (MoF figures in Fitch: 7.0% / 6.5% / 6.2% for 2025-27, debt ~70% of GDP by 2027); 2026 deficit cap PLN 271.7bn.",
   "fiscal_risk_text": "2026 needs ~38% (25 Feb) financed; budget accounts ~PLN 171.6bn at end-February. Moody's reviews Poland on 20 Mar (A2, negative).",
   "backdrop_text": "The NBP cut to 3.75% on 4 Mar after holding at 4.00% in January and February; January flash CPI 2.2%; 2025 GDP 3.6%, Q4 4.0%. Ratings: Fitch A- negative (affirmed 27 Feb), Moody's A2 negative, S&P A- stable. 4 Mar: the MPC cut all rates by 25bp (reference 3.75% from 5 Mar), citing geopolitical risk to commodity prices; the March projection (data to 19 Feb, war excluded) has 2026 CPI in a 1.6-2.9% band; ING called it a 'hawkish cut'; 2Y yields fell after the decision. Abroad: US ISM services 56.1, ADP +63k; Warsh's nomination went to the Senate."
  },
  "calendar": {
   "plan_text": "MoF March plan (27 Feb): sale auctions on 18 and 25 Mar (PLN 7-13bn each; OK0128, NZ0331, PS0731 (new 5Y fixed), DS1035, NZ0936 (new 10Y POLSTR floater)) and a switch on 11 Mar buying back OK0426, DS0726, PS1026, WZ1126 and OK0127; no T-bills; WZ sales ended in February. February sales were ~PLN 41bn; ~38% of 2026 needs financed.",
   "timing_text": "The Aug 2025-Feb 2026 pattern (auction-day close the cheapest point of the week) comes from a rally regime; in March's sell-off MoF is cutting supply (switch instead of sale, a smaller 25 Mar offer), so remaining dates (18 and 25 Mar) are less of a supply event. Next MPC 8-9 Apr: a hold is expected while the market prices hikes.",
